  "calibrated_on": "2026-10-27",
  "method": "Static HTML (homepage + 1 product page, stdlib urllib, normal browser UA, 1 request / 2 s) of 48 public stores, 28 of which expose Shopify webPixelsConfigList; vendor identity of Shopify app pixels confirmed by downloading the app pixel extension code (/web-pixels/strict/app/web-pixel-<id>@<scriptVersion>.js) on edikted.com; 3 GTM containers downloaded; 1 browser load (edikted.com) for collection endpoints. Raw files only under ~/STELLAR_OUTPUT/_tmp/house-skills-2026-10/fact-check-tags/.",
  "calibration_rule": "status=calibrated only if matched on >= 3 different real stores AND the matched snippet clearly identifies the vendor. Patterns are Python re, applied to raw HTML. Patterns inside webPixelsConfigList match the escaped JSON string (\\\" in HTML).",
  "false_positive_warning": "Bare domain strings (sc-static.net/scevent.min.js, analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js, s.pinimg.com/ct/core.js) were found inside cookie-consent inventories (OneTrust tag lists) and script-blocking regex lists on colourpop.com, princesspolly.com, us.ugreen.com. Never treat a bare domain hit as an installed tag; require code context (loader call / init call / script src) or the webPixelsConfigList entry.",
  "apiClientId_note": "apiClientId values are not documented by Shopify; mapping below is empirical (config keys + extension code). Re-check on every calibration run."
 },
